<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shashanka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 625</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shashanka was a king of Gauda in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> in the late 6th and early 7th centuries, often described as the first ruler to unite much of Bengal. From his capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnasuvarna">Karnasuvarna</a> he extended his power into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magadha">Magadha</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, and around 606 he killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajyavardhana">Rajyavardhana</a> of Thanesar, making <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harsha">Harsha</a> his lifelong enemy. Buddhist sources portray him as a persecutor; his gold coins show <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a> with the bull Nandi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shashanka.jpg" alt="Shashanka" width="320" height="151" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gauda_ruler_Sasanka_Deva._Circa_AD_600-635._Samatata_type._Assam_mint.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
